<title>BRAZIL: Brazil net dollar inflows at $74.8 mln April 22.</title>
<headline>Brazil net dollar inflows at $74.8 mln April 22.</headline>
<dateline>SAO PAULO 1997-04-23</dateline>
<text>
<p>Preliminary figures for Brazil's commercial and financial foreign exchange contracts showed a $74.8 million surplus on April 22 in the commercial forex market, according to Central Bank data suplied to banks.</p>
<p>A banker with access to the figures said the Central Bank</p>
<p>issued the following breakdown.</p>
<p>DOLLAR FLOWS ON APRIL 22</p>
<p>Exports: $222.5 million</p>
<p>Imports: $278.8 million</p>
<p>Finanancial buy: $277.8 million</p>
<p>Financial sell: $146.7 million</p>
<p>Net surplus: $74.8 million</p>
<p>APRIL DOLLAR FLOWS UP DATE</p>
<p>Exports: $3.181 billion</p>
<p>Imports: $3.424 billion</p>
<p>Financial buy: $4.273 billion</p>
<p>Financial sell: $3.637 billion</p>
<p>Net surplus: $393 million</p>
<p>Note: the figures were rounded off.</p>
<p>((--Alexandre Caverni, Sao Paulo newsroon, 55 11 2485418))</p>
</text>
